    {
      "id": "4e2b1b51-628e-47df-915a-b665a4c0e661",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### CTIS 210 Project 4: Methods that make decisions\n\nOne of the way in which programs are most useful is when they can choose to perform different actions as the information they have changes. \n\nA scenario that illustrates that point involves Guilford students registering for classes next semester. Each student's registration window opens at a time that is effectively based on two rules, which can be expressed using a point system.\n\n* At the time the first registration window opens, you are assigned a number of points based on the number of credits you have already **completed** with a passing grade. Your total credits include those taken at Guilford, credits transferred in, or credits assigned to you, such as for an AP exam score:\n    - 88 or more total credits: 4 points\n    - 56-87 total credits: 3 points\n    - 24-55 total credits: 2 points\n    - Fewer than 24 total credits: 1 point\n* If you are studying away from campus through a Guilford program, 5 additional points are added.\n\nThe more points you have, the earlier you get to register.\n\nIn this project, we'll now put that into practice using conditional logic.\n\nNote that you should run each code cell after making modifications to it. Don't continue to the next task until you are convinced that the code you've written so far is already working.\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "4e2b1b51-628e-47df-915a-b665a4c0e661"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4f29b618-bd97-49b6-8b11-3fce9d040014",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Initial setup task\n\nIn the following code cell, declare the following variables and assign them values as described.\n\n* A `String` variable with the identifier `studentName` and initialized with any name you choose.\n* A `String` variable with the identifier `gNumber` and initialized with a G number in standard format (\"G00\" followed by six digits).\n* Variables that hold the following decimal (floating-point) numbers:\n\n    |Description|Identifier|Initial value|\n    |:--|:--|:--|\n    |Credits earned at Guilford|`guilfordCredits`|36|\n    |Transfer credits|`transferCredits`|12|\n    |Other credits|`otherCredits`|4|\n    |Is the student studying away this semester?|`studyAway`|`false`|\n\nUse `System.out.println` or `System.out.printf` statements to display the information about the student in a nicely formatted way.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "4f29b618-bd97-49b6-8b11-3fce9d040014"
      }
    },
