    {
      "id": "d0a4551f-1a0c-4269-9a30-7734beb29c1d",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Comparison and logical expressions task\n\nTo make decisions, our program has to decide whether particular assertions are `true` or `false`. For example, we can assert \"The student has more than 56 or more credits completed at Guilford\". Based on the values provided at the beginning of this project, that assertion is `false`. In code, we would see that by examining the value of the **comparison** expression\n\n```java\nguilfordCredits >= 56\n```\n\nTest this assertion by writing the following statement in the next cell.\n\n```java\nSystem.out.println(\"Student has 56 or more Guilford credits: \" + (guilfordCredits >= 56));\n```\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "d0a4551f-1a0c-4269-9a30-7734beb29c1d"
      }
    },
    {
