    {
      "id": "6c7fd9a2-8717-4e75-a6e0-218e7a80451e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "We often need to test more complex assertions, like \"The student has fewer than 24 credits and is studying away\". Here's the **logical** expression that evaluates that assertion.\n\n```java\ncalcTotalCredits(guilfordCredits, transferCredits, otherCredits) < 24 && studyAway\n```\n\nIn the next code cell, write a statement like the previous ones that displays the evaluation of that assertion. Then, use comparison and logical operators to test the following assertions.\n\n* The student has at least 56 credits completed at Guilford or is not studying away.\n* The student has less than 8 other credits and more than 10 transfer credits.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "6c7fd9a2-8717-4e75-a6e0-218e7a80451e"
      }
    },
