      "id": "89eb8ec4-7c67-423b-951d-e2d3fc0793d5",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Conditional statement task\n\nA conditional statement allows the program to make decisions based on evaluating assertions. They use the keyword `if` and can also use the keyword `else`. An example is the following.\n\n>If the student has 88 or more total credits, give them 4 additional registration points. If they're studying away, give them 5 additional registration points.\n\nAnd here are the conditional statements that implement that.\n\n```java\ndouble registrationPoints = 0;\ndouble totalCredits = calcTotalCredits(guilfordCredits, transferCredits, otherCredits);\nif (totalCredits >= 88) {\n    registrationPoints = registrationPoints + 4;\n} \n\nif (studyAway) {\n    registrationPoints = registrationPoints + 5;\n}\n```\n\nAdd these conditional statements to the next code cell. Then, add a statement that prints out the value of `registrationPoints` with annotation.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "89eb8ec4-7c67-423b-951d-e2d3fc0793d5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "42a9264c-4180-4d89-bd16-3e1dcc3d3fe0",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Start the conditional statement task in this code cell\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2a65d7da-7d78-4018-b334-9cf2309f149e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "To continue this task, do the following in order.\n\n* At the beginning of the last code cell, assign the value 80 to `guilfordCredits`. Then run the code cell again to see the change in the value of `registrationPoints`.\n* Now assign the value `true` to `studyAway` at the beginning of that cell. Run the code cell again to see the change.\n\nVerify that the results are what you expect based on the current values of all the variables that affect the total number of points. ",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "2a65d7da-7d78-4018-b334-9cf2309f149e"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7577eabe-2ff4-49ef-b821-cac67f3020a7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "To continue this task, we want to add conditional statements that use all the rules that assign point values. For example, we have the rule\n\n* 56-87 total credits: Add 3 points\n\nThe logical expression to test that assertion is\n\n```java\ntotalCredits >= 56 && totalCredits <= 87\n```\n\nFollowing the pattern in the code cell above, add three conditional statements to that code cell that implement the remaining rules. Modify the values of the variables such as `guilfordCredits`, `otherCredits`, and `transferCredits` so that you're fully testing that your rules work as expected.\n\n*Optional*: There are two ways to add the additional conditions. What I describe here has you use additional `if` conditional statements. You can also use the `else` keyword to build more complex conditional statements. Either approach is fine as long as the code does what it's supposed to and you can explain how it works.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "7577eabe-2ff4-49ef-b821-cac67f3020a7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4972f1ff-5a48-4658-9e64-fcfd0257fc1d",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Building a point calculation method task\n\nOne issue that we have now is that it's difficult to easily use our code to calculate points for many students without repeating the code we already have. That's becomes a reason to put all the point calculation into a method. \n\nWe've done almost all the hard work. We just need a full method definition. \n\nThe signature will be\n\n```java\npublic double calculatePoints()\n```\n\nBe sure you can identify each component of the signature.\n\nHere's what to do next. Copy all of the code in the last code cell ***except*** for any statements that display information or change values of the credit and `studyAway` variables. Paste that code into the next cell in the specified location. Run the code cell to make sure there are no errors (but you won't see anything yet).",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "4972f1ff-5a48-4658-9e64-fcfd0257fc1d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fb88d646-8428-4ec0-9219-a727d1d2fa98",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Build the point calculation method here\npublic double calculatePoints() {\n    // Paste the code below this line\n\n\n    \n    // And above this line\n    return registrationPoints;\n}\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
